// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - LoyalistHero 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2760452801" "{HeroName}, I'm here on behalf of Provost Marchand to help make your transition into Primal Earth a smooth one. He commends your choice for moving forward to help keep the peace in Praetoria.<br><br>There are a few things you need to know before going into Primal Earth."
// Answer Text :
"P3469403457" "What do I need to know?"
// Page Washington Text :
"P1649200853" "Primal Earth is a somewhat more... <i>chaotic</i> place than Praetoria. Specifically, Paragon City is faced with many threats on a daily basis. We will be placing you in the center of the action, as they say, in a place called <color yellow>Talos Island</color>. There, you will be on your own to help protect the people of Paragon and prove that we are a force of <i>good</i>. I will give you a quick combat analysis of some of the groups you will be facing in Paragon City."
// Answer Text :
"P3600698197" "Alright, who will I be facing?"
// Page McKnight Text :
"P4034448239" "One of the chief threats, as you may have seen already, is Arachnos. I'm sure you're fairly familiar with them. Next we have two warring groups, the Council and the 5th Column. Both seek complete domination of the world and have attempted to do so numerous times.<br><br>The two groups are constantly fighting each other in Paragon and many innocent civilians are dragged into their battles. Taking the fight to them will help lower the chaos and destruction that Cole sees in Primal Earth."
// Answer Text :
"P323696466" "Who else will I be facing?"
// Page Ivy Text :
"P2217531891" "There is the Freakshow, a group of anarchists who love nothing more than destruction. I assume you're seeing a pattern here, correct? They fight with cybernetic implants and constantly recruit those youths in Paragon who share their same ideals. As you can see, the youth in such a world are worse off than our own.<br><br>Here, they only risk being recruited by the Resistance. In Primal Earth, nearly every major group seeks to bolster their ranks by manipulating those too naive to see through their lies. I should mention, also, that Primal Earth also faces a threat that we are all too familiar with: Hamidon."
// Answer Text :
"P1835154093" "Hamidon is in Primal Earth as well?"
// Page Reese Text :
"P241526361" "Yes, though it is contained to a place called the 'Hive'. At least, the center of the beast is. Many of its creatures roam through Paragon City, seeking to destroy the very fabric of it. I sincerely believe it is only a matter of time until they face the same catastrophic events that we encountered during the Hamidon Wars.<br><br>Those are the main groups you should be aware of.<br><br>If you find yourself in Paragon City and do not have anyone direct to help, you can check a <color yellow>police scanner</color> that you will receive when you go through. The scanner will allow you to pick up any crimes in the area that are happening. As you can see, their police force is much more... loose than ours in handling crime. By following the scanner long enough, you will surely be able to find the source of a major plot by one of the <i>hundreds</i> of villains running rampant in Paragon. Doing so will gain you the attention of a number of people who could use your help. It's a primitive way of doing things, but that's why we call them Primals."
// Answer Text :
"P1895440208" "Understood. Anything else I should be aware of?"
// Page End Text :
"P4169671379" "Only one thing. We have intelligence to believe that there is a group on the other side called SAM who are already on the look out for you. It appears there is someone who looks exactly like you causing chaos in Primal Earth.<br><br>I would seek out this agent as soon as you enter Talos and put a stop to this as soon as you can. Clearly, someone is aware that we seek to improve the image of Praetoria in Paragon and is moving against us as we speak."
// Answer Text :
"P3563830222" "I'll make sure to do that."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ResistanceVillain 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3562395092" "IGNORE RESISTANCE VILLAIN PAGE FOR THE LOYALIST MISSION. I'M KEEPING THIS HERE AS A BACK UP."
// Answer Text :
"P1103471647" "Ricochet is alive"
// Answer Text :
"P4062398753" "Ricochet is captured"
// Page Ricochet Text :
"P1911634309" "You've got Ricochet. Splice?"
// Answer Text :
"P863729748" "Splice is here."
// Answer Text :
"P4178379470" "Splice isn't here."
// Page NoRicochet Text :
"P1735532039" "You don't have Ricochet. Splice?"
// Page Splice Text :
"P404809024" "You've got Splice. Jackhammer?"
// Answer Text :
"P763742723" "Jack is here."
// Answer Text :
"P2249309859" "Jack is not here."
// Page NoSplice Text :
"P4156512598" "You've got McKnight. Ivy?"
// Page Jack Text :
"P2970682408" "You've got Jack. Beholder and Hatchet?"
// Answer Text :
"P1745063572" "They're here."
// Answer Text :
"P3040937076" "Not here."
// Page NoJack Text :
"P2727989206" "You've got Ivy. But now, the question is, were you a Powers guy who went all the way through then chose hero?"
// Page Beholder Text :
"P2371604990" "You saved Beholder"
// Answer Text :
"P1196501531" "End"
// Page NoBeholder Text :
"P2001109640" "You didn't Save Reese."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - LoyalistVillain 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1769633867" "{HeroName}, I see you've chosen to go to the Rogue Isles. I'm with you in your thoughts, believe me. Primal Earth is full of nothing but chaos and destruction, but it doesn't mean that it isn't ripe for opportunity.<br><br>I'll give you a brief rundown of what you can expect when you go through to the Rogue Isles."
// Answer Text :
"P3330739927" "Alright then."
// Page MrG Text :
"P4151208154" "The Rogue Isles are 'ruled' by Arachnos. I use that term in the loosest sense possible, given how powerful our Emperor Cole is. You will, unfortunately, have to deal with them many times while you are in the Rogue Isles. Luckily, we have an agent on the inside, one you will meet shortly. But suffice to say, you will have to put up with a lot from this organization while you are in the Isles.<br><br>Just know, however, that they are all beneath you and every single Praetorian that inhabits this city."
// Answer Text :
"P2241213222" "I'll keep that in mind. What else?"
// Page Riptide Text :
"P3405349305" "If you find yourself lacking someone to... let's say, 'help you move forward', you can use the newspaper in the Rogue Isles to look for plenty of opportunities. These can range from simply beating down anyone who would seek to take you down to stealing valuable items to use for yourself. Doing enough of these tasks will lead you to people who you can properly use to further your own power within the Rogue Isles, though I would keep my eye on them. They all think like Primals and would try to take advantage of you just as soon as you'd take advantage of them."
// Answer Text :
"P900360775" "So, I will have no allies in the Rogue Isles?"
// Answer Text :
"P1055902738" "Anything else I need to know?"
// Answer Text :
"P2639011566" "Understood. Anything else?"
// Page PowersTeam Text :
"P3594232596" "You may have some allies, yes. You can try to build your own base of power, but I would be careful. Many have tried, but only few have succeeded. Even if you do so, you may be seen by our great Emperor as a threat to be disposed of when the invasion happens."
// Answer Text :
"P3112090498" "I'll bear that in mind. Anything else?"
// Page End Text :
"P1997460530" "That would be it. We have an ally of ours waiting on the other side of the rift. Proceed through to meet with them."
// Answer Text :
"P515170056" "I'll do that."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ColeTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2361469883" "Hello, {HeroName}. I have to say, it's surprising to see one of the Powers Division here in Primal Earth. I can only assume that Marchand wants to make an attempt to form peace here."
// Answer Text :
"P1743312768" "Emperor Cole? What are you doing here?"
// Page DoingHere Text :
"P3243928608" "That is my own business, {HeroName}. I have to wonder, however, about your own loyalty to Praetoria. Are you truly fine with putting our fair city at risk of being invaded first by these creatures of destruction in Primal Earth?"
// Answer Text :
"P3927125471" "I've killed good people in the name of Praetoria, Cole. Don't question -my- loyalty."
// Answer Text :
"P756848224" "My own loyalty? You have -no- idea, Cole, what I've been through."
// Page KilledPeople Text :
"P3523717873" "And yet here you are now, seeking to stop more deaths from happening. Your hands are already stained with blood, {HeroName}, much like mine. But we both have done all of these things to protect what we believe in, to protect Praetoria.<br><br>That is why I fought Hamidon, to protect the world. <i>That</i> is why I have made Praetoria as it is today, to protect the people from themselves."
// Answer Text :
"P1903139631" "From themselves?"
// Page Noidea Text :
"P3169570355" "I believe I can have some semblance of what you've been through. Much like myself, I imagine. Hardships, pains, difficulties. And all of it was in the name of Praetoria, was it not? To protect the people, to protect the city?<br><br>I have done all the same, {HeroName}, only for myself, it was to protect the world. That is why I stepped forward to save this world from Hamidon, and that is why I have taken such measures to protect the people of Praetoria from the chaotic nature of humanity."
// Answer Text :
"P4048873709" "You're protecting the people from themselves?"
// Page ColeLecture Text :
"P1784229170" "Yes, {HeroName}. People are weak, at least when it comes to doing the right thing. That is why you cannot give them the choice to do what is <i>wrong</i>. I have done so in Praetoria, and look at how it has flourished. Primal Earth, however, allows this to continue, even with some of the <i>worst</i> examples of humanity. That is why it must be wiped away. They know of our perfect world and already, as you have seen, they seek to destroy it.<br><br>People, when left to their own free will, will seek only to destroy that which is good, that which is pure, {HeroName}. I will not give them the option to do that. I will strike them down before they can act and ensure that no others ever get the chance to make that choice, the choice to destroy. Humanity cannot be trusted with that choice of destruction; only someone like myself can."
// Answer Text :
"P848973853" "Maybe you don't believe in humanity anymore, Cole, but I still do."
// Answer Text :
"P1364393834" "They may be weak, Cole, but they deserve a chance to live."
// Page Humanity Text :
"P3501996516" "<color orange>Cole smiles for a brief moment before his face returns to a neutral expression.</color><br><br>You remind me of myself, {HeroName}, so long ago. I, too, once believed that humanity was good, that it could band together and be saved from the horrors that it was capable of. But this isn't true, {HeroName}. I have learned this the hard way. You, too, shall learn this the hard way as well. Your time on Primal Earth will show you the true nature of humanity. That I am sure of."
// Answer Text :
"P231177448" "And what are you going to do?"
// Page Achance Text :
"P3092482763" "Those who are in Praetoria deserve the chance to live, {HeroName}. But not the people in Primal Earth. They have gone for far too long believing in their own way of life. I cannot simply just go in there and have them change. No, doing so would be far too difficult and would risk the lives of those in Praetoria.<br><br>The only way this can end is for all those in Primal Earth who <i>can</i> stand against me to be wiped out. The others will be assimilated into the new Praetorian society on Primal Earth. I will not hesitate to have my army turn on you, {HeroName}, if you choose to fight on the side of Primals. But I believe that your time in Primal Earth will show you the true, rotting nature of humanity and the horrors that it's capable of."
// Answer Text :
"P3264455293" "And you? What are you going to do?"
// Page You Text :
"P3213257673" "I have other matters to attend to, {HeroName}. This will be the last time you will see me for some time. When we meet again, it will either be with you by my side as we enter Primal Earth, or you staring down one of the War Walkers. Make your choice wisely."
// Answer Text :
"P203766940" "I already have, Cole."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ViridianTalk 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1069555862" "Hello. You would be {HeroName}, correct? Good to meet you.<br><br>I am <color yellow>Viridian</color>, spymaster for Arachnos and the head of Project: Praetoria. Not the most creative of titles, but I'm not a man who is concerned about 'creativity'. I've been informed that you wish to enter the Rogue Isles. I am in place to help bring you in."
// Answer Text :
"P1677443419" "I'm not working for Arachnos, if that's what you're proposing."
// Page Working Text :
"P47045028" "I don't imagine you'd work for anyone, {HeroName}. I'm here to ensure that Arachnos remains a lucrative ally for you and any other Praetorian that is coming through to Primal Earth. I'm well aware of your Emperor Cole's plans for an invasion. To have you <i>not</i> on his side will benefit all of us in the end."
// Answer Text :
"P805462873" "So, what are you going to offer me?"
// Page Offer Text :
"P3325779978" "First, the title of 'Destined One'. I've put your name into the list that <color yellow>Kalinda</color> has. Not a real difficult thing for me to accomplish, as you may imagine. Being a Destined One within the Rogue Isles will grant you certain priveleges and also a certain air of power. Some in Arachnos will respect you for it, though most will still be willing to bash your head in.<br><br>You can do whatever you want with this title. Ignore it, go along with it, or anything. But it is yours, should you wish to utilize the benefits that come with it."
// Answer Text :
"P4094083014" "Fair enough. What else?"
// Page WhatElse Text :
"P1598354648" "I've seeded word of your name into various groups that work within the Rogue Isles. Though they may not have encountered you, they already believe you're a force to be reckoned with. It may not be the best start, but there is a man who will help you get started on your path in Sharkhead Isle. His name is <color yellow>Dean MacArthur</color>. He will be able to get you whatever it is you want as you get started within the Isles."
// Answer Text :
"P1614547382" "Alright. And what about you?"
// Page AboutYou Text :
"P1125886108" "Myself? I'll be working from the shadows, {HeroName}. Perhaps in the future, you and I will work together. There is a lot going on behind the scenes in this project of mine, much of which is not exactly... fully revealed to the Arbiters.<br><br>Should an opportunity arise that can benefit both you and myself, I will contact you. But for now, I shall keep your true origin a secret, so long as you agree to keep this little meeting of ours secret. Lord Recluse is not extremely happy with the idea of Praetorians in the Rogue Isles, given how Cole operates. It is best to keep your true nature a secret until you've built up enough power.<br><br>Oh, and just so we keep this formal. Welcome to the Rogue Isles."
// Answer Text :
"P3266421093" "... Thanks."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - WashingtonDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2685335751" "You've done a lot for Praetoria, {HeroName}. I know it wasn't easy for you to help me with Cleopatra, but it had to be done.<br><br>I believe Praetor White has recovered from the incident after speaking with Emperor Cole, though I tend not to go too close to him. You understand, I'm sure. At any rate, I wish you the best of luck in Primal Earth. I hope that you can do what you can to prevent a war from breaking out. There are a lot of good men and women in the PPD. I wouldn't want to see their lives lost if there is a peaceful way around things.<br><br>Just remember, there may come a point where you can't do anything else to help those people. When that time comes, you'll need to do what's best for Praetoria."
// Answer Text :
"P566634965" "I'll do my best, Washington."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ChanceDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2699041990" "We've been on a very difficult path, haven't we, {HeroName}? I hope that you can do what you can to prevent this war with Primal Earth.<br><br>As for me? I've been assigned to a special squad to deal with various issues that spring up with the Syndicate. It looks like I'll never be able to break myself away from them, eh? Let's hope that one day you'll come back from Primal Earth, {HeroName}. We'll have a drink and talk about what we've both seen on each side."
// Answer Text :
"P3477828750" "Stay safe, McKnight."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - IvyDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2611460642" "I have helped two hundred and forty five people since we last spoke, {HeroName}! Provost Marchand wants to extend his thanks to you for activating my programs to act freely to aid the people of Praetoria! I also have the following messages that have been given to me when I have informed people that you re-programmed my systems!<br><br>'Thank you, {HeroName}! You saved my husband's life!<br><br>'I thought those monsters were going to kill me! If you hadn't changed IVy, I would've never survived to see my children!<br><br>'IVy helped us stop a Resistance bombing plot before it was too late. It's good to know we can rely on it and members of Powers Division to help us out.'"
// Answer Text :
"P3295803707" "Thank you, IVy."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ReeseDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P589827039" "Hello, {HeroName}. It's been a while, hasn't it?"
// Answer Text :
"P1309181780" "Reese? What are you doing here?"
// Page Page1 Text :
"P3405116174" "Easy, I'm not here to fight you.<br><br>I survived our last fight on that rooftop, but barely. I crawled my way into the tunnels and clung to life, fighting off all the monsters that lurked in the shadows. I honestly thought I was going to die, until I was taken in by some of the tunnel dwellers. I figured they didn't know who I was, that's the only reason why they were helping me.<br><br>Turns out, they knew <i>exactly</i> who I was and still wanted to help me. That's when it all changed, {HeroName}. They nursed me back to health and I helped get them back to the surface. I've been staying under the radar with the help of Provost Marchand. He told me that you were going to be leaving for Primal Earth today, so I stopped by.<br><br>I... wanted to apologize to you, {HeroName}, for everything. For Warrant... for trying to kill you, well, <i>multiple</i> times. I'm trying to change now, {HeroName}. If you're going to go fight the good fight in Primal Earth, then I'm going to fight the good fight here in Praetoria."
// Answer Text :
"P2387796613" "Just don't slip back to your old self, Reese."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MrGDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P4195212925" "Hello, {HeroName}. I'm pleased to see that you've made it this far in your journey through Praetoria, quite pleased. I'm here to wish you good luck in your trip to the Rogue Isles. I've heard much about the place, it sounds interesting, very interesting indeed.<br><br>I do hope that you and I will be seeing each other again one day. That is all, {HeroName}, I'll be keeping this brief. Much to do, so much to do before this day is over."
// Answer Text :
"P2719524348" "Goodbye, Mr. G"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - RiptideDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2008338579" "Going to the Rogue Isles, huh? Wish I could go there with you, {HeroName}. I'm eager to prove myself against all those scum that walk around in there. Do me a favor and take a few down for me. Hopefully one day, I'll get the same chance you have now to go over there and carve out a path for myself."
// Answer Text :
"P583094482" "Maybe one day, Riptide."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - AriaDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3054764901" "Good luck over in the Isles, {HeroName}. Ever since that close call with Reese, I've been keeping myself low-key in Nova Praetoria, doing small work with Praetor White. I still haven't gotten back to my full power since the attack, but perhaps one day I will.<br><br>Once that day comes, maybe you and I can do some damage in the Rogue Isles, hm?"
// Answer Text :
"P1218315415" "We'll see about that, Aria."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ZaneDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1164060647" "Can't say I envy you going over to the Rogue Isles, {HeroName}. Place seems like a dump compared to Praetoria. But, I guess it does have more opportunity than we do here. You can't exactly have your own base of operations here without Cole approving of it, can you?<br><br>At least in the Rogue Isles, Arachnos and Recluse aren't too efficient at keeping people in line."
// Answer Text :
"P2199962047" "That's one of its good points, I'll say."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - SternDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P688050862" "I don't totally approve of you going to the Isles, {HeroName}. But I am sure you will eventually do something useful there. After all, you chose to save us instead of going after that girl in the Resistance.<br><br>In the meantime, when we meet again, I shall have more of my parts replaced. Praetor White has enlisted me in one of Berry's new programs to enhance my combat abilities."
// Answer Text :
"P1752231165" "Good luck with that, Stern."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2610693727" "{HeroName}, as I'm sure you're fully aware, Emperor Cole is planning on a massive invasion into Primal Earth.<br><br>As commander of the military, I would like to do my best to avoid any sort of conflict if we can. I know nearly every member of our military, at least the <i>human</i> ones, by name. If I can avoid putting them in harms way, all the better. It is why I want you to act as an ambassador of sorts for us in Primal Earth.<br><br>They all believe that all Praetorians are evil, that we seek to destroy them. With that mentality, it will be impossible for us to avoid any kind of war, which is exactly what Emperor Cole believes. However, if we can show them that not all of us are evil, that we are just simply <i>concerned</i> about their chaos, then perhaps peace can be made.<br><br><color yellow>Completing this mission will send your character into Primal Earth and out of Praetoria. If you have any other business to finish in Praetoria, now would be the time to do it.</color>"
// AcceptString :
"P487506225" "How would I get to Primal Earth?"
// SendOffString :
"P222694206" "Through the <color yellow>Rift Enclosure</color> beneath Keyes Island. It is one of the many projects that Anti-Matter has been working on. We currently have two portals beneath there. One of them leads to a location in <color paragon>Paragon City</color>, the other goes into the <color red>Rogue Isles</color>. The choice of where you go is up to you, though I would heavily suggest going to Paragon City. They will be the ones that can be more easily convinced that we are on <i>their</i> side, that some of us here in Praetoria do not wish to wipe them all out.<br><br>The Rogue Isles, on the other hand, is a place where only scum and villainy live. Arachnos will not see any reason, not until they are destroyed. To go to the Rogue Isles would not help anyone but yourself; it is only a place where one would go to seek to increase their own power.<br><br>I implore you to make the right choice, {HeroName}, if you truly care for the safety of Praetoria and Primal Earth."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3750750329" "Go through the Rift Enclosure (Single Player)"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P152677503" "I cannot make the choice for you, {HeroName}. I can only hope you make the best choice possible."
// TaskTitle :
"P2906544022" "<color deepskyblue>The Rift Enclosure</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P560138819" "You travel deep beneath the Keyes Island before you arrive to this room, the crossroads between the portal to Paragon City and the portal to the Rogue Isles."

